      "name": "MiniMax H3 Text to Video (10Eros Max + Turbo)",
      "icon": "⚡",
      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-turbo-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "The 10Eros Max finetune paired with the v4-600 EMA Turbo LoRA at 6 steps. **The fastest preset in this collection.**\n\nMeasured 67.9s at 5s/480p/6 steps on SimpliGen 1.50.0 / engine v0.33.1, a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti and ~19 GB system RAM free — 1.70x the official 20-step preset. Re-measured 2026-08-27 on the beta engine warm at seed 77777: 66.6s against stock 113.2s. The earlier 1.82x was against a slower stock baseline (123.5s), not a faster turbo.\n\nThe Turbo LoRA composes cleanly with this non-pruned base, which was not obvious in advance. Its adaln update lives in the 2688-dim silu(t_emb) space and is re-injected at runtime on to the adaln projection's OUTPUT (96768 wide on both the stock pruned base and this one), so the differing input compression never enters into it. Verified in practice: the node reports the LoRA active with 47 patches attached and a clean RMS trajectory.\n\nNote: on long, detail-heavy prompts the app's accelerator toggles can cost more time than they save on this hardware. If a 15s character-and-dialogue prompt runs slower than you expect, try turning Spectrum and Sol-Attn off — output was indistinguishable in testing and it measured roughly twice as fast without them.",
